# ── build output & dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
dist-electron/
release/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.local

# ── secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── the assistant's working directory ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Local tooling only: it is symlinked to repos that exist on one machine, so shipping it
# would hand the next person dangling links, and it is no part of the application.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, and that is not cosmetic. `.claude/` matches a directory and nothing else,
# so the day this became a SYMLINK to the single shared copy — one source of truth for this
# working copy and the clone beside it — git stopped ignoring it and offered to commit the link
# itself. A bare `.claude` matches the directory, the symlink, and a plain file of that name.
.claude
CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json

# ── documents ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignores NEW files under `docs/` — the review reports, renders and snapshots this project
# generates locally and does not want offered for commit on every `git status`.
#
# What it does NOT do, and this is the part worth knowing: `.gitignore` has no effect on a file
# git is already tracking. `docs/PLAN.md`, `docs/WORK-BREAKDOWN.md`, `docs/design/DESIGN-BRIEF.md`
# and the architecture PDF stay tracked, stay in a fresh clone, and are still what the README
# links to. Editing them still shows up as a change.
#
# The cost, recorded rather than left to be discovered: a document somebody genuinely wants in
# the repository from now on has to be added with `git add -f`, and until they do, nothing will
# mention that it is missing.
docs/

# ── the notes the app writes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent reads and writes here at runtime. It is user data, not source.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and that is not cosmetic: an unanchored `notes/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so it silently swallowed `src/infrastructure/notes/` —
# the adapter for this very folder. Everything still built here, because the file exists here;
# a clone had no such file and did not compile. `npm run verify:clone` is what found it.
/notes/
!/notes/.gitkeep

# ── editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.log
